{
  "name": "Energy",
  "entries": [
    {
      "name": "Coal Generator",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "card",
          "icon": "industrial_core:coal_generator",
          "title": "Coal Generator"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Your first generator. It burns any fuel; a coal block burns longer and gives more. It pushes power out on every side by itself, so put machines and cables right next to it."
        },
        {
          "type": "items",
          "items": [
            "industrial_core:coal_generator"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Solar Panels",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "card",
          "icon": "industrial_core:solar_panel_t1",
          "title": "Solar Panels"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "They run on their own as long as they see open sky. Full output by day, a quarter at night."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "There are ten tiers and each is far stronger than the last. The first is made of silicon, and the tenth, the Dyson panel, is the most powerful generator in the mod."
        },
        {
          "type": "items",
          "items": [
            "industrial_core:solar_panel_t1",
            "industrial_core:solar_panel_t4",
            "industrial_core:solar_panel_t7",
            "industrial_core:solar_panel_t10"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Panel Combiner",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "card",
          "icon": "industrial_core:panel_combiner",
          "title": "Panel Combiner"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Instead of laying out a field of panels, put them in the **combiner**: it holds up to 18 panels and outputs their combined power from one block. The combiner itself must see the sky."
        },
        {
          "type": "items",
          "items": [
            "industrial_core:panel_combiner"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Cables",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "card",
          "icon": "industrial_core:copper_cable",
          "title": "Cables"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Cables carry power from generators to machines. Each one has a limit on how much it passes per tick. In order: copper, ferro, gold, crystalline, emerald, heavy, and netherite fiber, which has almost no limit."
        },
        {
          "type": "stats",
          "rows": [
            {
              "key": "Copper cable",
              "value": "4,096 FE/t"
            },
            {
              "key": "Ferro cable",
              "value": "65,536 FE/t"
            },
            {
              "key": "Gold conductor",
              "value": "262,144 FE/t"
            },
            {
              "key": "Crystalline channel",
              "value": "1,048,576 FE/t"
            },
            {
              "key": "Emerald flux cable",
              "value": "4,194,304 FE/t"
            },
            {
              "key": "Energy magistral",
              "value": "16,777,216 FE/t"
            },
            {
              "key": "Netherite fiber",
              "value": "no limit"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "tip",
          "text": "The bare wire for the energy magistral only comes from **wire cutters**, out of a redstone block."
        },
        {
          "type": "items",
          "items": [
            "industrial_core:copper_cable",
            "industrial_core:ferro_cable",
            "industrial_core:gold_conductor",
            "industrial_core:crystalline_channel",
            "industrial_core:emerald_flux_cable",
            "industrial_core:heavy_magistral",
            "industrial_core:netherite_fiber_cable"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Batteries & Cells",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "card",
          "icon": "industrial_core:battery",
          "title": "Batteries & Cells"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You carry them in your inventory: they charge your tools and armor and let you take power with you. From smallest to largest: battery, lithium battery, flux core and plasma core."
        },
        {
          "type": "items",
          "items": [
            "industrial_core:battery",
            "industrial_core:lithium_battery",
            "industrial_core:flux_core",
            "industrial_core:plasma_core"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Energy Bank",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "card",
          "icon": "industrial_core:energy_bank",
          "title": "Energy Bank"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A big 10M FE battery block. In its window you set how many percent to keep in reserve, and everything above that goes back into the grid. It also shows how much power comes in and out."
        },
        {
          "type": "items",
          "items": [
            "industrial_core:energy_bank"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Battery Charger",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "card",
          "icon": "industrial_core:battery_charger",
          "title": "Battery Charger"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Put a battery, cell or tool inside, run a cable to it, and it charges the item from the grid."
        },
        {
          "type": "items",
          "items": [
            "industrial_core:battery_charger"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}